&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 13.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: -13.5pt; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 9pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri; font-size: 6pt; vertical-align: super;"&gt;(1)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;Our exposure to credit losses for certain regulated utility customers is mitigated by a regulatory mechanism we have in place. Specifically, our residential tariffs include a mechanism for cost recovery or refund of uncollectible expense based on the difference between actual uncollectible write-offs and the amounts recovered in rates. As a result, at June&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;30, 2026, $128.4 million, or 54.9%, of our net accounts receivable and unbilled revenues balance had regulatory protections in place to mitigate the exposure to credit losses.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
